{"h": {"measure": "A", "k": 100}, "sp": "nb", "rep": 136, "hyps": [{"edit_edge": 3, "edit_op": "skip_connect", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "Adding a residual where no direct input-output path existed yields large gains (exps 1, 5, 9), far above replacing an existing op."}, {"edit_edge": 3, "edit_op": "skip_connect", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "direction": "lower", "why": "Replacing a 3x3 conv on the direct path loses capacity, giving the smallest or negative gains (exps 2, 6, 10, 14, 18)."}, {"edit_edge": 3, "edit_op": "skip_connect", "cond_edge": 0, "cond_op": "avg_pool_3x3", "direction": "lower", "why": "In parameter-free pooling cells, an extra skip further dilutes the signal and hurts badly (exps 13-16)."}, {"edit_edge": 3, "edit_op": "skip_connect", "cond_edge": 0, "cond_op": "skip_connect", "direction": "lower", "why": "In all-skip cells, adding another identity path degrades accuracy heavily (exps 17-20)."}, {"edit_edge": 4, "edit_op": "skip_connect", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "When edge 3 is missing, a skip on edge 4 supplies the residual shortcut and helps much more (exps 65-68, 73-76 vs 61-64, 69-72)."}, {"edit_edge": 4, "edit_op": "skip_connect", "cond_edge": 0, "cond_op": "avg_pool_3x3", "direction": "lower", "why": "Swapping the only conv out for a skip in pooling-dominated cells removes almost all learnable capacity (exps 79-80)."}, {"edit_edge": 0, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 4, "cond_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "direction": "lower", "why": "Deleting edge 0 starves the conv on edge 4, so removal hurts more than when edge 4 is none (exps 42, 45, 54, 56 vs 41, 44, 53, 55)."}, {"edit_edge": 5, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 1, "cond_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "direction": "higher", "why": "A conv on edge 5 is more useful when node 2 receives rich conv features from edge 1 (exps 29-36 vs 21-28)."}, {"edit_edge": 1, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 5, "cond_o